**Sub-lemma (S2/S3, L-mono).** Define $[\![M]\!]_\rho\in\mathcal V_\sigma$ for $M:\sigma$ and environment $\rho$ by structural recursion:
- $[\![x]\!]_\rho=\rho(x)$;
- $[\![MN]\!]_\rho=[\![M]\!]_\rho([\![N]\!]_\rho)$;
- $[\![\lambda x.M]\!]_\rho=$ the functional $a\mapsto[\![M]\!]_{\rho[x:=a]}$ **plus a strict inflationary $+1$ increment** on the weight.

Prove by induction on $M$ that $[\![M]\!]_\rho$ is **strictly** (not merely weakly) monotone in every free variable, and that the increment keeps the abstraction inside $\mathcal V_{\sigma\to\tau}$ (still strictly monotone).

**Why hard.** (i) Strictness, not weak monotonicity, is needed for the reduction-in-argument case (G6); many proofs only get the weak form. (ii) The application case must propagate strict monotonicity through functional application. (iii) The increment must be compatible with the closure conditions defining $\mathcal V_{\sigma\to\tau}$.
